# ============================================================================
# .github/CODEOWNERS — mandatory review for the code that moves money (P1).
#
# GitHub matches the LAST pattern that applies, so the ordering below is
# deliberate: broad defaults first, then progressively narrower
# high-blast-radius areas.
#
# ─────────────────────────── BEFORE THIS WORKS ──────────────────────────
# Replace every @org/team placeholder with real teams or usernames, then
# enable branch protection on `main`:
#
#   Settings → Branches → main →
#     [x] Require a pull request before merging
#     [x] Require review from Code Owners
#     [x] Require status checks: "App workspace", "Security",
#         "Deployment config", "Frontend"
#     [x] Do not allow bypassing the above settings
#
# CODEOWNERS WITHOUT BRANCH PROTECTION IS A SUGGESTION, NOT A CONTROL.
# An auditor will check the branch-protection setting, not this file.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- default ---
